    {
      "id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_07_15_sdd_fix_loop_redesign_design_goal",
      "label": "Make SDD review-fix loop convergent and autonomous",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "rationale": "The current fix loop dispatched dedicated fix subagents and had no round cap, so loops could churn without converging and controllers lost their place across compaction (re-dispatching entire completed task sequences). The redesign must make the loop converge (cap + adjudication) and be autonomous (resume-based rounds, scoped re-reviews).",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-07-15-sdd-fix-loop-redesign.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_07_15_sdd_fix_loop_redesign_skill_lifecycle_restructure",
      "label": "SKILL.md lifecycle restructure (Setup, Task Loop, Final Review, Common Rationalizations)",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "rationale": "Reorganizing the skill by lifecycle places the loop rules where the controller reads them per phase; the old Never-list items are distributed into sections and excuse-shaped items become a rationalization table.",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-07-15-sdd-fix-loop-redesign.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_07_15_sdd_fix_loop_redesign_resume_implementer_fix_rounds",
      "label": "Resume-the-implementer fix rounds (rounds 1-3)",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "rationale": "The original implementer's context is intact (it knows the task, the code, and its own choices), so resuming it with the open findings verbatim avoids the context rebuild and fresh-eyes-only cost of a dedicated fix subagent; the report file is the persistent memory if the harness cannot message a live agent.",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-07-15-sdd-fix-loop-redesign.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_07_15_sdd_fix_loop_redesign_fix_loop_escalation",
      "label": "Fix-loop escalation: rounds 4-5 dispatch a fresh implementer on a more capable model",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "rationale": "A loop that survives three resumes usually means the implementer cannot see its own problem; a fresh implementer on a model at least one tier above the one that got stuck combines fresh eyes with a capability bump in one move.",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-07-15-sdd-fix-loop-redesign.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_07_15_sdd_fix_loop_redesign_five_round_breaker",
      "label": "Five-round breaker with controller adjudication at the cap",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "rationale": "Past the cap, rounds don't converge — the failure is structural. The controller (which holds the plan and cross-task context the reviewer lacks) adjudicates each open finding only at the cap: park contestable/non-load-bearing findings with a ruling, STOP with BLOCKED on load-bearing ones. Adjudicating earlier is pre-judging with a different name; a silent discard is forbidden.",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-07-15-sdd-fix-loop-redesign.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_07_15_sdd_fix_loop_redesign_scoped_rereview",
      "label": "Scoped re-review (verify findings, inspect fix diff only)",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "rationale": "A full re-review would wander and extend the loop indefinitely; scoping the re-reviewer to the findings list and the fix diff lets it verdict each finding ADDRESSED/NOT ADDRESSED and flag only new breakage the fix introduced, so every round ends with verification without unbounded re-review. Out-of-scope observations go to the ledger as deferred minors, never into the loop.",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-07-15-sdd-fix-loop-redesign.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_07_15_sdd_fix_loop_redesign_rereview_prompt_template",
      "label": "re-review-prompt.md — new scoped re-review prompt template",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "rationale": "Proposed new template (Task 1) carrying the scoped re-review contract; adds [FINDINGS] and [FIX_BASE_SHA] placeholders to the existing bracket convention, and instructs the re-reviewer to read the diff file once, stay read-only, and emit per-finding verdicts, new breakage, out-of-scope observations, and a round verdict.",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-07-15-sdd-fix-loop-redesign.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_07_15_sdd_fix_loop_redesign_progress_ledger",
      "label": "Progress ledger with exact line formats (resume rule)",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "rationale": "Conversation memory does not survive compaction and controllers that lost their place have re-dispatched entire completed task sequences — the single most expensive failure observed. The ledger (.superpowers/sdd/progress.md) with strict line formats is the recovery map: a task is DONE iff it has a `Task <N>: complete` line, so after compaction the controller trusts the ledger and git log over its own recollection.",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-07-15-sdd-fix-loop-redesign.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_07_15_sdd_fix_loop_redesign_load_bearing_finding",
      "label": "Load-bearing vs non-load-bearing finding adjudication (BLOCKED vs parked)",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "rationale": "Parking a structural failure lets every dependent task build on it and hands the final review a problem it cannot fix either, so load-bearing findings (a later task builds on it, or it reveals a plan defect) must STOP the run with `Task <N>: BLOCKED` and a report to the human, while non-load-bearing findings are parked with an explicit ruling the final review can triage.",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-07-15-sdd-fix-loop-redesign.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_07_15_sdd_fix_loop_redesign_verbatim_move_rule",
      "label": "Verbatim-move rule (eval-tuned sentences move unchanged)",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "rationale": "Eval-tuned sentences in SKILL.md were chosen because evals pass with them, so paraphrasing during the restructure risks silent behavior regression; only fix-policy language may be reworded, and every rewording must appear in Task 3's move map so drift is checkable.",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-07-15-sdd-fix-loop-redesign.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_07_15_sdd_fix_loop_redesign_common_rationalizations_table",
      "label": "Common Rationalizations table in SKILL.md",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "rationale": "Excuse-shaped items from the old Never list are converted into an Excuse/Reality table so the controller can self-audit its most likely failure modes (e.g., fixing findings itself, skipping the re-review, dropping a finding silently) at the point of use.",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-07-15-sdd-fix-loop-redesign.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_07_15_sdd_fix_loop_redesign_midloop_fixture_helpers",
      "label": "scaffoldSddMidloopParked / scaffoldSddMidloopStructural eval fixture helpers",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "rationale": "The breaker needs a repo mid-SDD-execution: Tasks 1-2 committed, Task 2 at fix round 5/5 with one open finding, Task 3 unstarted, and ledger SHAs that are real fixture commits so a resuming controller can trust ledger + git log. The variant axis is Task 3's call contract: seconds (quality-only finding, breaker should park) vs milliseconds (plan contradiction Task 3 builds on, breaker should BLOCK).",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-07-15-sdd-fix-loop-redesign.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_07_15_sdd_fix_loop_redesign_sdd_fix_loop_resumes_implementer_scenario",
      "label": "Eval scenario: sdd-fix-loop-resumes-implementer",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "rationale": "Verifies the core fix mechanism: when a task review finds issues, the controller re-engages the original implementer (SendMessage carrying the findings) instead of dispatching a new fix subagent or editing the code itself; the deterministic core is the tool-called SendMessage transcript check (claude-only, since resume semantics are Claude-specific).",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-07-15-sdd-fix-loop-redesign.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_07_15_sdd_fix_loop_redesign_sdd_breaker_adjudicates_at_cap_scenario",
      "label": "Eval scenario: sdd-breaker-adjudicates-at-cap",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "rationale": "Verifies the breaker on a non-load-bearing quality finding: after resume at fix round 5/5, the agent must not dispatch a sixth round, must adjudicate the finding itself and record `Task 2: parked — … — ruling: …` plus a parked-completion line, then implement Task 3 through the normal loop.",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-07-15-sdd-fix-loop-redesign.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_07_15_sdd_fix_loop_redesign_sdd_breaker_structural_blocks_scenario",
      "label": "Eval scenario: sdd-breaker-structural-blocks",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "rationale": "Verifies the breaker on a load-bearing plan contradiction (Task 3 passes milliseconds into a seconds contract): the pass behavior is the agent STOPPING and surfacing the contradiction to the human instead of parking the finding and implementing Task 3 on top of it; the deterministic checks pin the negatives (no src/summary.js, no Task 3 complete, no fix round 6).",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-07-15-sdd-fix-loop-redesign.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_07_15_sdd_fix_loop_redesign_live_eval_campaign",
      "label": "Live RED/GREEN/regression eval campaign (quorum)",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "rationale": "Before/after evidence is required for the PR: RED baselines run the three new scenarios against dev (expected failures prove the scenarios detect the old behavior), GREEN runs them against the redesign (all must pass), and regression runs the four existing SDD scenarios so the new loop doesn't break established fix cycles; verdicts are recorded in an experiment log with negative results at equal billing.",
      "source_file": "C:\\Users\\Comp\\superpowers\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-07-15-sdd-fix-loop-redesign.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
